B.

Skyrmion-Antiskyrmion tunneling

We will now consider the consequences of skyrmionantiskyrmion tunneling. Using that 1/Θ in Eq. (13) is
expected to be much larger than the exponentially small
tunneling rate, we assume in the following that the magnetization of the skyrmion is fixed to its ground state
value. The effective Hamiltonian for the tunneling problem is therefore given by
