skyrmion is located.
For Nf = 2 mod 3 we obtain numerically that the
tunneling from the lowest Landau level of the skyrmion
and the antiskyrmion is not possible, δk = 0. We have
not been able to find an analytic argument proving this.
To calculate the band-structure in this case, we therefore
have to consider Landau-level mixing induced by the tunneling process. We have used a discretized version of the
Hamiltonian (18) to calculate numerically the resulting
bandstructure. As is shown in Fig. 8, the bandwidth is
proportional to the square of the (exponentially small)
tunneling rate δ in this case and thus much smaller than
for Nf = 0, 1 mod 3 where a dispersion linear in δ was

