Classical approximation for the lattice potential

In order to estimate the prefactor V0 of the lattice potential we can employ a classical approximation of the
magnetization by replacing the quantum mechanical spin
operators S in the Hamiltonian, Eq. (1), with classical
Heisenberg spins m with kmk = 1/2. We can exploit
that the skyrmion position is fixed by symmetry if it is
initialized on a highly symmetric point. Thus we use
standard relaxation algorithms without artificially fixing
any spins to calculate the energy of a skyrmion which is
centered (i) on a lattice site, (ii) on a plaquette, and (iii)
on a bond between lattice sites, respectively. Although
we only require the energies of two positions for fitting
V0 , we can use the third position to validate the simplified
ansatz for the potential, Eq. (A1).

